<p><a href="/mail/<%= message.id %>">← Original customer email</a></p><h1>Review customer return email</h1>
<p>An RMA authorizes the customer to send these goods back. It does not confirm receiving them, add stock, change an invoice or pay a refund.</p>
<% if(locked){ %><p class="notice"><span class="badge">Growth</span> Return requests from email need Growth with approval or training, or Pro / Custom for routine work. <a class="btn" href="/billing">Upgrade</a></p><% } %>
<% if(shadow){ %><p class="notice">The first 14-day watch period is active. You can review the source; agent requests wait until it ends.</p><% } %>
<section class="card"><div class="card-body"><h2>Original request</h2><p>From <%= message.sender %> · <%= message.subject %></p><div style="white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere"><%= message.body_text %></div></div></section>
<% if(!locked){ %>
<form method="get" class="form-stack"><label for="return-inspection-location">Location for the later physical inspection</label><select id="return-inspection-location" name="locationId" required><option value="">Choose an internal location</option><% for(const place of places){ %><option value="<%= place.id %>" <%= selected===place.id?'selected':'' %>><%= place.name %></option><% } %></select><button class="btn">Preview return request</button></form>
<% if(morePlaces){ %><p>Showing the first 250 active internal locations. Choose the inspection site for this request.</p><% } %>
<% if(problem){ %><p class="notice"><%= problem %></p><% } %>
<% if(prepared){const p=prepared.facts; %><section class="card"><div class="card-body"><h2><%= prepared.existing?'Recorded RMA':'Exact proposed RMA' %></h2><p><%= p.customerName %> · Order <%= p.orderNumber %></p><p>Requested resolution: <%= {REFUND:'Refund requested — requires later approval',EXCHANGE:'Exchange requested — requires later approval',NO_REFUND:'No refund requested'}[p.input.resolution] %></p><p>Reason: <%= p.input.reason %></p><p>Customer return reference: <%= p.requestReference||'None provided; individual approval required' %></p>
<ul><% for(const line of p.lines){ %><li><%= line.quantity %> <%= line.unit %> · <%= line.code %> · <%= line.name %></li><% } %></ul>
<% if(policy){ %><p>Return value: <%= policy.value||'Unknown' %><% if(policy.limitText){ %> · ask above <%= policy.limitText %><% } %></p><p>Goods left <%= policy.days===null?'on an unknown date':policy.days+' day'+(policy.days===1?'':'s')+' ago' %><% if(policy.window!==null){ %> · return window <%= policy.window %> days<% } %></p>
<% const outside=policy.problems.filter(x=>!/^Save your return window/.test(x)); if(outside.length&&!prepared.existing){ %><p class="notice"><%= outside.join(' ') %></p><% } %><% } %>
<% if(prepared.existing){ %><p><strong><%= prepared.existing.return_number %></strong> · <%= prepared.existing.status %></p><a class="btn" href="/returns/<%= prepared.existing.customer_return_id %>">Open this RMA</a>
<% }else{ %><form method="post" class="form-stack"><input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>"><input type="hidden" name="locationId" value="<%= p.locationId %>"><input type="hidden" name="expectedFingerprint" value="<%= p.sourceFingerprint %>"><label><input type="checkbox" name="confirmed" value="yes" required> I approve this original customer request, order, products, quantities and requested resolution.</label><% if(policy&&policy.problems.some(x=>!/^Save your return window/.test(x))){ %><label><input type="checkbox" name="policyConfirmed" value="yes" required> I accept this return even though it is outside my return policy.</label><% } %><button class="btn" <%= shadow?'disabled':'' %>>Create this RMA</button></form><% } %>
</div></section>
<% if(canTeach){ %><section class="card"><div class="card-body"><h2>Teach this customer and product scope</h2><p>Growth needs this reviewed example before handling the same customer, products, mailbox, location and requested resolution. A lower rule limit also applies on Pro and Custom.</p>
<form method="post" action="/mail/<%= message.id %>/return-rule" class="form-stack"><input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>"><input type="hidden" name="revision" value="<%= rule?.revision||0 %>"><label>Maximum whole units in each matching request<input type="number" name="maximumUnits" min="1" max="100000" step="1" value="<%= rule?.maximum_units||p.lines.reduce((n,line)=>n+line.quantity,0) %>" required></label><label><input type="checkbox" name="confirmed" value="yes" required> I approve this exact customer and product rule, within the maximum above.</label><button class="btn" <%= shadow?'disabled':'' %>>Save return request rule</button></form></div></section><% } %>
<% } %>
<section class="card"><div class="card-body"><h2>Routine returns from incoming email</h2><p>After you turn this on, Pro and Custom create RMAs from clear emails by known customers. Growth also needs a matching taught rule. Requests outside your return window, above your high-value limit, for an unknown order or for items not on the order wait for you in Needs you. Receiving the goods and refunds keep their own approvals.</p>
<form method="post" action="/mail/<%= message.id %>/return-settings" class="form-stack"><input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>"><input type="hidden" name="revision" value="<%= setting?.revision||0 %>"><label for="routine-return-location">Inspection location</label><select id="routine-return-location" name="locationId" required><option value="">Choose an internal location</option><% for(const place of places){ %><option value="<%= place.id %>" <%= (setting?.quarantine_location_id||selected)===place.id?'selected':'' %>><%= place.name %></option><% } %></select>
<label>Maximum whole units per request<input type="number" name="maximumUnits" min="1" max="100000" step="1" value="<%= setting?.maximum_units??'' %>" required></label>
<label>Return window in days<input type="number" name="windowDays" min="1" max="3650" step="1" value="<%= setting?.window_days??'' %>" required></label>
<label>Ask me about returns worth more than (<%= currency %>)<input type="text" inputmode="decimal" name="reviewAbove" value="<%= reviewAboveText %>" required></label><input type="hidden" name="currency" value="<%= currency %>">
<label><input type="checkbox" name="confirmed" value="yes" required> I authorize clear return requests from known customers within these limits.</label><button class="btn" <%= shadow?'disabled':'' %>>Enable routine RMA requests</button></form>
</div></section>
<% } %>
<% if(setting?.enabled){ %><form method="post" action="/mail/<%= message.id %>/return-settings"><input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>"><input type="hidden" name="revision" value="<%= setting.revision %>"><button class="btn" name="stop" value="yes">Stop routine RMA requests</button></form><% } %>
<% if(rule&&evidence?.customer_return_id){ %><form method="post" action="/mail/<%= message.id %>/return-rule"><input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>"><input type="hidden" name="revision" value="<%= rule.revision %>"><label><input type="checkbox" name="confirmed" value="yes" required> I confirm removing this learned limit. The plan's routine settings still apply.</label><button class="btn" name="remove" value="yes">Remove this learned return rule</button></form><% } %>
